   }
  ]
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Write $f=g\\circ j$ with $j\\colon X\\to W$ an open immersion and $g\\colon W\\to Y$ affine, using\n[lemma-nagata-zmt-open-immersion-affine-factorization]. An affine\nmorphism to a quasi-affine scheme has quasi-affine source, so $W$ is\nquasi-affine. Moreover $X$ is quasi-compact, since $f$ is quasi-compact and\n$Y$ is quasi-compact. So $X$ is a quasi-compact locally closed subscheme of\nthe quasi-affine scheme $W$, and such a subscheme is quasi-affine (Stacks Tag\n0BCK).",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-zmt-open-immersion-affine-factorization"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
